{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Children that are born to them, a third generation, etc.</b> And other nations are permitted immediately. Thus you have learned that causing a person to sin is harder upon him than killing him — for killing him kills him in this world, but causing him to sin removes him from this world and from the World to Come. Therefore Edom, who came against them with the sword, was not abhorred, and likewise Egypt, who drowned them — but these, who caused them to sin, were abhorred (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:04.960360090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}